=head1 NAME

_CALCULATE_INTERPOLATED_OPACITY_ - Get an opacity value for a frequency

=head1 DESCRIPTION

This primitive interpolates the ITC-style opacity data files found in
the C<cal/acsis/itcdata> directory.  There is a selection of files
for different 225 GHz opacities.  First the pair of files either side
of the given 225 GHz opacity is found (using a list of filenames
present in this primitive).  Then each file is interpolated to obtain
an opacity value for the given frequency.  Finally we interpolate
between these two values to obtain an estimate for the desired conditions.

(This primitive is based on the heterodyne ITC's get_interpolated_opacity
method, which itself was based on the corresponding routine in HITEC.)

=head1 PARAMETERS

=over 4

=item OPACITY (Returned)

The interpolated opacity value.

=item OPACITY_225 (Given)

Opacity at 225 GHz.

=item FREQ_GHZ (Given)

Frequency in GHz.

=back

